  "subsystem": {
    "name": "VehiclePhysics",
    "responsibility": "Vehicle configuration loading (.SVM/.HDV line parsing into an internal setup struct plus a normalized output vehicle-state struct) and physics dynamics-matrix identity initialization.",
    "trust": "DERIVED",
    "evidence_refs": [
      "function:0x004F4270",
      "function:0x00578F76",
      "abi:lead"
    ]
  },
  "summary": "Two functions. ParseSvmHdvVehicleConfigFile (0x004F4270) is a line-by-line .SVM/.HDV parser owned by TheSvmHdvVehicleFileParser (DERIVED from the legacy ABI lead): it opens the file in binary-read mode, validates the format on a first pass, dispatches each named section (General, FrontWing, LeftFender, RightFender, RearWing, BodyAero, Diffuser, Suspension, Controls, Engine, Driveline, per-wheel corners, Basic) to a section reader, resolves secondary files (damage model, engine, gear file, physical model, tire compound) relative to the config path, and normalizes range/setting pairs into the output vehicle state. InitPhysicsTransformIdentity (0x00578F76) is a selector dispatch (0..33) that initializes one row of a large double-precision physics dynamics matrix block (0x008D2120..0x008D3978) to an identity row (diagonal 1.0, off-diagonals 0.0), returning the selector argument.",
